# Verify after code changes

When implementation is complete, **run and test** before ending the turn — do not only describe what to run.

## Required workflow

1. **Build or compile** — e.g. `npm run build`, `dotnet build`, or equivalent for the touched stack.
2. **Run targeted tests** — unit tests and/or E2E for the changed area; fix failures before finishing.
3. **Smoke the app** when UI/routing/auth changed — start dev servers if needed, hit critical paths (login, navigation).
4. **Stop dev servers** on ports 3000/5180 when done (see agent-testing-lifecycle rule).

## When to skip

- User explicitly asked for plan/review only with no code changes.
- Environment blocker after retry — report what failed and what remains unverified.

## Reporting

Summarize: build result, tests run (pass/fail counts), and any unverified items.
